<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31837" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obsĕro</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		ob-sera, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to bolt, bar, fasten</i>, or <i>shut
				up</i> (not in Cic. or Cæs.; syn.: claudo, oppilo,
			obstruo). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ostium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Eun. 4, 6, 25</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aedificia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 5,
					41</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fores (opp. aperire),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Tit. 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tabellam liminis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					32, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exitus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					9, 1, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rogos,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the dead</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					4, 11, 8</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aures,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					Epod. 17, 53</span></i>
			: palatum (for os), i. e. <i>to be
				silent</i>, <i><span class="en">Cat. 55, 21</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fores amicitiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 27, 12</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
